I've finished the maintainer session. The site build passes and both repos are pushed: site commit `6a13ba7`, research commit `a850db9e`.

**WAKE: two findings that reach past the site**
- **The modified-gravity reading of dark energy fails lunar laser ranging.** A visitor persona raised this as HIGH, and I checked it with a script before writing anything. If the coupling G/C(ρ̄) is the G that holds the Earth and Moon together, it drifts as the universe thins out: Ġ/G = 3(1−Ω_m)H₀ ≈ 1.4×10⁻¹⁰ per year. Lunar laser ranging measures (7.1 ± 7.6)×10⁻¹⁴ per year. That is about 2,000× too large, and at least 527× beyond the 2σ edge for every γ from 0.3 to 3. The script's three predictions, written before it ran, all held. So any reading where G/C affects local gravity is now excluded, whether keyed on local or on mean density. Only the ordinary dark-energy-fluid reading (Cardassian-class) survives. No bucket moves and the count stays at 6.
- **A three-month-old result never reached the site.** The 08-02 null (local density adds nothing once g_bar is known) sat in the explorer's findings and no page carried any of its numbers. I drained it, and also asked the explorer to measure how many other findings were never drained, by searching the site for each finding's numbers. Filenames turned out to be a bad proxy for this.

